codex
I found an important design cue in the supplied semantics: concrete `split()` is defined, while symbolic string proofs are explicitly expected to intercept `split` problem-locally. I’m following that model—concrete runs will use the real reference rules, and the general proof will use a narrowly scoped sentence/token abstraction while still executing the translated function body, indexing, conversions, and arithmetic.
