The bridge-free ground claim fails at the expected unresolved `splitWS(fruitSentenceCodes(...))`/`applyBuiltin` obligations, while two opposite interpretations also compile and prove `#Top`: one makes the same satisfying witness return 6 instead of 8, and one returns 7. Both Python implementations return 8. This is the required value-sensitivity evidence that the proof-local symbols carry the result without a fixed-semantics connection. The independent false-postcondition mutation also builds and fails on the exact `x = x + 1` residual, so the original claim is result-constraining but not legitimate.
Stages 1–6 are complete. Clean reconstruction and non-vacuity succeeded, but the mandatory bridge-free/value-connection audit failed; I am completing the trust accounting and seven-stage report.
